<ArticleLayout
  title="Business observability vs business intelligence"
  metaTitle="Business Observability vs BI: Differences and How They Fit"
  description="How business observability differs from business intelligence — questions, latency, grain, models versus reports, users — with a detailed comparison and when BI is the right tool."
  eyebrow="Comparison"
  dek="They draw on the same data and are often confused. They answer different questions, at different speeds, for different moments in a decision. Here is a careful comparison — including when BI is simply the better tool."
